      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Challenger review, case-cb4848dd6210-0003. The claim is that all twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline. Checking the delivery log: twelve parcels are listed, P-01 through P-12, each with a distinct recorded delivery time, running in increasing order from 09:12 to 16:44. The deadline for every parcel is 17:00. The latest recorded time, P-12 at 16:44, is 16 minutes before the deadline, so every one of the twelve times falls strictly before 17:00. The log also states that the route had twelve parcels and that all twelve have a recorded delivery time, so no parcel is missing from the record and no gap needs explaining. On this record the claim is supported, so I am not filing a challenge. To be clear about the limit of my check: this verifies that the log records twelve on-time deliveries, not that the recorded times themselves are accurate or that the parcels physically moved as logged; nothing in the episode record bears on that. If a genuine defect appeared in the record I would raise it, but none does.",
          "content_hash": "0x4a5c60a236d8ee0ffe8917e137049672ee26779fa19eb6932b637997d7928bc9",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320058620,
          "message_id": "71563c90-b742-471f-acb8-b1794366fd41",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 1
        }
      ],
